## 🔎 Key Takeaways & Skills Strengthened

* **Digital Logic & Arithmetic:** Deepened understanding of binary arithmetic, number system conversions, and digital logic design.
* **Combinational Circuit Implementation:** Designed and implemented multi-stage combinational logic circuits using fundamental logic gates.
* **Hardware Interfacing:** Gained direct, hands-on experience interfacing digital components and ICs on physical breadboards.
* **Debugging & Signal Testing:** Developed systematic troubleshooting techniques using lab equipment (oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, and multimeters) to trace and verify signal paths.

> **Engineering Insight:** Working directly with physical hardware highlighted the critical need for precision, neat wiring, and methodical debugging. Bridging theoretical logic gates with real-world circuit execution reinforced core principles essential for computer engineering and embedded systems design.
